body:
I really love Things 3. I&#39;ve been around the block when it comes to productivity apps, and Things simply does it best. However, I&#39;m very disappointed on the fact it&#39;s not available on the web or other platforms. As a user who integrates both Apple and Windows into my life, I find trying to stick to Things 3 a bit of a pain. I have a macbook, I have an iPhone, however at home I use my Windows PC most of the time. Anytime I have reached out to Cultured Code, I always get the same basic and unheartfelt response &#39;There&#39;s no plans for that at the moment, but thanks for letting us know you like it.&#39;

Their responses almost feel very robotic. You&#39;ll notice by going through their replies on Social Media, it&#39;s almost all the same mundane responses to people asking questions. I strongly dislike that the company behind the app does not share anything that&#39;s on the roadmap for Things. I&#39;d sooner pay a subscription model to be able to use this on other platforms.

It&#39;s not all negative though. The app itself is beautiful. I love how they don&#39;t constantly add new features, as this could have easily ruined the app. I do however feel the app is slacking in comparison with its competitors. All I ask is PLEASE be more transparent with your service users.
